567
00:20:21,400 --> 00:20:22,460
And this reframing

568
00:20:22,460 --> 00:20:23,120
is brilliant.

569
00:20:23,860 --> 00:20:24,340
Fliction says

570
00:20:24,340 --> 00:20:25,500
we completely misunderstand

571
00:20:25,500 --> 00:20:27,120
what buffer inventory

572
00:20:27,120 --> 00:20:28,300
actually is.

573
00:20:28,900 --> 00:20:29,060
Right.

574
00:20:29,160 --> 00:20:30,840
Because in modern business,

575
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:31,580
we are taught

576
00:20:31,580 --> 00:20:33,360
that having extra inventory

577
00:20:33,360 --> 00:20:34,680
sitting on a warehouse shelf

578
00:20:34,680 --> 00:20:35,640
