00:20:36,100 --> 00:20:37,480
It's expensive slack.

580
00:20:37,800 --> 00:20:39,320
It's a waste of working capital,

581
00:20:39,580 --> 00:20:40,800
a waste of floor space.

582
00:20:41,320 --> 00:20:42,120
But Fliction says

583
00:20:42,120 --> 00:20:43,380
no, that physical buffer

584
00:20:43,380 --> 00:20:44,400
is a system's

585
00:20:44,400 --> 00:20:45,660
local repair capacity.

586
00:20:45,660 --> 00:20:47,360
It is the literal

587
00:20:47,360 --> 00:20:48,340
physical ability

588
00:20:48,340 --> 00:20:49,760
of that specific warehouse

589
00:20:49,760 --> 00:20:51,760
