this perfectly

1467
00:37:35,580 --> 00:37:36,380
onto the concepts

1468
00:37:36,380 --> 00:37:37,020
of repair

1469
00:37:37,020 --> 00:37:38,320
and admissibility.

1470
00:37:38,760 --> 00:37:39,720
During the day,

1471
00:37:39,840 --> 00:37:40,640
as you experience

1472
00:37:40,640 --> 00:37:41,160
the world,

1473
00:37:41,580 --> 00:37:42,780
you encode new,

1474
00:37:43,080 --> 00:37:44,160
highly fragile memories

1475
00:37:44,160 --> 00:37:45,800
in a seahorse-shaped

1476
00:37:45,800 --> 00:37:46,620
part of the brain

1477
00:37:46,620 --> 00:37:47,720
called the hippocampus.

1478
00:37:47,880 --> 00:37:48,880
But the hippocampus

1479
00:37:48,880 --> 00:37:49,560
is small.

1480
00:37:49,800 --> 00:37:51,280
It's just temporary storage.

1481
00:37:51,740 --> 00:37:52,760
It learns fast,

1482
00:37:52,840 --> 00:37:53,980
but it forgets fast.

1483
00:37:54,180 --> 00:37:56,080
During slow-wave NREM sleep,

1484
00:37:56,160 --> 00:37:56,880
that deep sleep,

1485
00:37:56,940 --> 00:37:57,540
early in the night,

1486
00:37:57,720 --> 00:37:58,560
your brain enters

1487
00:37:58,560 --> 00:37:59,940
a massive repair phase.

1488
00:38:00,640 --> 00:38:02,300
It selectively reactivates

1489
00:38:02,300 --> 00:38:03,260
those fragile traces

1490
00:38:03,260 --> 00:38:04,280
in the hippocampus

1491
00:38:04,280 --> 00:38:05,360
to see if they should be

1492
00:38:05,360 --> 00:38:06,100
moved to the cortex

1493
00:38:06,100 --> 00:38:07,320
for long-term storage.

1494
00:38:07,580 --> 00:38:08,480
And this reactivation

1495
00:38:08,480 --> 00:38:09,380
isn't just a metaphor.

1496
00:38:09,860 --> 00:38:10,660
There is a literal,

1497
00:38:10,880 --> 00:38:12,620
physical, electrical dialogue

1498
00:38:12,620 --> 00:38:13,620
happening in the brain.

1499
00:38:13,620 --> 00:38:15,920
It is incredibly precise.

1500
00:38:16,540 --> 00:38:17,160
Researchers like

1501
00:38:17,160 --> 00:38:18,220
Bernhard Stericina

1502
00:38:18,220 --> 00:38:19,240
have mapped

1503
00:38:19,240 --> 00:38:20,280
a hierarchical nesting

1504
00:38:20,280 --> 00:38:21,220
of brain waves

1505
00:38:21,220 --> 00:38:21,800
that looks like

1506
00:38:21,800 --> 00:38:23,080
a perfectly timed

1507
00:38:23,080 --> 00:38:24,180
biological orchestra.

1508
00:38:24,800 --> 00:38:26,940
You have slow oscillations

1509
00:38:26,940 --> 00:38:27,880
in the cortex,

1510
00:38:28,320 --> 00:38:29,260
providing a massive,

1511
00:38:29,780 --> 00:38:31,040
rhythmic up-and-down beat.

1512
00:38:31,280 --> 00:38:32,260
Nested perfectly

1513
00:38:32,260 --> 00:38:33,740
inside the up-states

1514
00:38:33,740 --> 00:38:34,700
of those slow waves

1515
00:38:34,700 --> 00:38:36,180
are faster bursts

1516
00:38:36,180 --> 00:38:37,240
of electrical activity

1517
00:38:37,240 --> 00:38:38,600
called sleep spindles.

1518
00:38:38,840 --> 00:38:39,800
And nested perfectly

1519
00:38:39,800 --> 00:38:40,820
inside those spindles

1520
00:38:40,820 --> 00:38:42,200
are incredibly fast,

1521
00:38:42,340 --> 00:38:43,160
sharp-wave ripples

1522
00:38:43,160 --> 00:38:44,400
coming from the hippocampus.

1523
00:38:44,500 --> 00:38:45,520
So the hippocampus

1524
00:38:45,520 --> 00:38:46,940
is firing rapid bursts

1525
00:38:46,940 --> 00:38:47,580
of information

1526
00:38:47,580 --> 00:38:49,020
directly into the open windows

1527
00:38:49,020 --> 00:38:50,140
provided by the cortex.

1528
00:38:50,620 --> 00:38:50,900
Yes.

1529
00:38:51,340 --> 00:38:51,920
And during those

1530
00:38:51,920 --> 00:38:53,220
tiny, sharp-wave ripples,

1531
00:38:53,700 --> 00:38:55,440
the actual waking experiences

1532
00:38:55,440 --> 00:38:56,320
of your day

1533
00:38:56,320 --> 00:38:57,480
are being replayed.

1534
00:38:57,660 --> 00:38:57,840
Yeah.

1535
00:38:58,100 --> 00:38:58,800
Matthew Wilson

1536
00:38:58,800 --> 00:38:59,760
and Bruce McNaughton

1537
00:38:59,760 --> 00:39:00,900
did these classic,

1538
00:39:01,260 --> 00:39:02,240
mind-blowing studies

1539
00:39:02,240 --> 00:39:02,920
with rodents.

1540
00:39:03,040 --> 00:39:03,700
They recorded

1541
00:39:03,700 --> 00:39:04,920
the exact neuronal

1542
00:39:04,920 --> 00:39:05,940
firing patterns

1543
00:39:05,940 --> 00:39:06,920
in a rat's brain

1544
00:39:06,920 --> 00:39:07,660
while it was learning

1545
00:39:07,660 --> 00:39:08,940
to run a physical maze.

1546
00:39:09,040 --> 00:39:09,260
Then,

1547
00:39:09,500 --> 00:39:10,300
when the rat fell asleep,

1548
00:39:10,300 --> 00:39:10,880
they saw those

1549
00:39:10,880 --> 00:39:11,820
exact same neurons

1550
00:39:11,820 --> 00:39:12,820
firing in the exact

1551
00:39:12,820 --> 00:39:13,520
same sequence

1552
00:39:13,520 --> 00:39:14,720
just much faster.

1553
00:39:14,960 --> 00:39:15,800
The brain was running

1554
00:39:15,800 --> 00:39:16,420
the maze again

1555
00:39:16,420 --> 00:39:16,960
in its sleep.

1556
00:39:17,120 --> 00:39:17,960
And later research

1557
00:39:17,960 --> 00:39:19,100
by Gabrielle Girardot

1558
00:39:19,100 --> 00:39:19,560
showed that

1559
00:39:19,560 --> 00:39:20,660
if you use technology

1560
00:39:20,660 --> 00:39:21,960
to selectively suppress

1561
00:39:21,960 --> 00:39:23,360
just those specific

1562
00:39:23,360 --> 00:39:24,240
sharp-wave ripples,

1563
00:39:24,640 --> 00:39:25,840
the rat doesn't remember

1564
00:39:25,840 --> 00:39:27,060
the maze the next day.

1565
00:39:27,520 --> 00:39:28,320
So Enrem sleep

1566
00:39:28,320 --> 00:39:29,620
is literally cross-checking

1567
00:39:29,620 --> 00:39:30,380
these new memories

1568
00:39:30,380 --> 00:39:31,660
against your existing

1569
00:39:31,660 --> 00:39:32,500
cortical network.

1570
00:39:32,720 --> 00:39:33,560
It's asking

1571
00:39:33,560 --> 00:39:34,720
the admissibility question.

1572
00:39:35,220 --> 00:39:36,700
Is this memory important?

1573
00:39:37,060 --> 00:39:37,820
Is it admissible?

1574
00:39:37,820 --> 00:39:39,300
Can we integrate

1575
00:39:39,300 --> 00:39:40,280
this new fact

1576
00:39:40,280 --> 00:39:41,780
into long-term storage

1577
00:39:41,780 --> 00:39:43,180
without destabilizing

1578
00:39:43,180 --> 00:39:43,920
the whole system?

1579
00:39:44,160 --> 00:39:44,480
Exactly.

1580
00:39:44,680 --> 00:39:45,460
It's an active filter.

1581
00:39:46,180 --> 00:39:46,760
And then we have

1582
00:39:46,760 --> 00:39:47,460
REM sleep,

1583
00:39:47,640 --> 00:39:48,540
the dreaming phase.

1584
00:39:48,940 --> 00:39:49,760
Fliction calls REM

1585
00:39:49,760 --> 00:39:50,800
the commit phase.

1586
00:39:51,300 --> 00:39:52,020
By the time you get

1587
00:39:52,020 --> 00:39:53,160
to the heavy REM cycles

1588
00:39:53,160 --> 00:39:53,960
later in the morning,

1589
00:39:54,220 --> 00:39:55,340
Enrem has already done

1590
00:39:55,340 --> 00:39:55,960
the heavy lifting

1591
00:39:55,960 --> 00:39:57,360
of filtering and reactivating.

1592
00:39:57,680 --> 00:39:59,000
REM takes the memory traces

1593
00:39:59,000 --> 00:40:00,040
that actually survive

1594
00:40:00,040 --> 00:40:00,960
